adaptation-samsung-beyond2lte (18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * droidian-quirks-regenerate-ssh-keys next to openssh-server: openssh-server
    is installed while the image is built, so its host keys are created
    then, and every phone flashed from the same image would share them.
    The quirk makes new ones on the first boot.
  * The USB cable network is rndis-usb, enabled from the first boot, and it
    creates the g1 gadget itself.  hybris-usb is dropped again: its
    usb-tethering cannot set up a network function on this kernel and
    leaves a failed unit; 17 depended on it without it ever working.
    The phone is at 169.254.172.1 (link-local, no DHCP needed; Windows
    loads its RNDIS driver by itself through the Microsoft OS descriptors).

